x axis is absolute log exposure in lux-seconds (daylight), as printed with bar notation (3.0 with an overbar = -3.0), axis -4.0 to 1.0; the curves are drawn from about -3.42 to about 0.58. Printed 'Log H Ref: -1.44'. The sheet also has a second plot 'Characteristic Curves, EI 800 (Push 1)' with the same Log H Ref, which is not traced.","Spectral sensitivity: effective exposure 1/50 s, density 0.2 above D-min, Status M; y is log sensitivity (reciprocal exposure in erg/cm2) as printed, and on this sheet the axis runs -1.0 to 3.0 (not 0.0 to 4.0). The yellow-forming (b) curve starts at about 380 nm, the magenta-forming (g) at about 395 nm, the cyan-forming (r) at about 485 nm and ends at about 695 nm; the g curve has a blue shoulder (about 0.9 to 1.2) before its green peak.","Spectral-dye-density plot has only 'Midscale Neutral' (mid, drawn dashed) and 'Minimum Density' (min), no separate c/m/y dyes; the dashed curve is read through its dashes. Both curves start at 400 nm already high (mid about 1.9, min about 1.4) and fall steeply.","Printed checks (Status M red-filter densities of a normally exposed negative, EI 400): grey card 0.80 to 1.00; lightest paper-gray-scale step 1.15 to 1.35. At EI 800 (push 1): 1.00 to 1.20 and 1.40 to 1.60. The modulation transfer function plot is not traced.","Grain: Print Grain Index for 135 at 4x6 print (39); 8x10 = 61, 16x20 = 90. The sheet says the film is optimized for printing on Kodak Professional Portra Endura, Supra Endura and Ultra Endura Papers, Duraflex Plus Digital Display Material and Endura Metallic Paper."],"print":"kodak-endura-premier","grain":{"grain":18.9,"grain_size":32.0,"grain_roughness":50.0}}